  "limitations": [
    "A same-turn reversal is A→B→A, including deliberate retracing. Longer cycles also count as revisits.",
    "No-move/no-offense turns may include deliberate Dodge, healing, or resource actions. Casting an attack that gets saved still counts as an offensive choice.",
    "Full-HP Second Wind is useful for Tactical Shift only from level 5 and with immediately following movement.",
    "Already-lethal rider detection considers pending damage and remaining HP plus temporary HP. It excludes Monk and Rogue opponents because their pending damage reductions can be private.",
    "Shield tradeoff eligibility checks for injured Wizard/Sorcerer, available reaction and spell slot, inactive Shield, surviving even maximum dagger critical damage, and opponent action unspent. It cannot determine which action would follow, whether a Shield-relevant hit would occur, or the effect of declining an opportunity.",
    "Ground-target summaries compare the chosen tile to legal geometry, not damage rolls. Caltrops placements do not establish a successful trap or tactical value."
